    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><fw place="top" type="adressline">Mrs. <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3454"
                            type="person">W. G. Sawitz</rs>
                        <lb/>250 E. Johnson St. <lb/><rs ref="#tillich_place_id__747" type="place"
                            >Philadelphia</rs> 44, <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__998" type="place"
                            >Pa.</rs></fw><dateline><date when="1946-02-04">Feb. 4,
                        1946</date></dateline><salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928"
                            type="person">Professor Tillich</rs>:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>I am somewhat concerned over the whereabouts of <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__2737" type="person">Dorothee Poelchaus</rs> letter
                    which I sent to you on <date when="1946-01-02">January 2nd</date>.<note
                        type="ea">Liegt nicht vor.</note> I never heard whether it reached you and
                    whether you sent it back to me. I sincerely hope it was not lost somewhere
                        <foreign xml:lang="fra">en route</foreign>. I did not even copy the Swiss
                    adress before sending it off to you. Please don&apos;t mind my asking about it. It
                    would be a pity if it had gone astray, but maybe we could still trace it. If you
                    did not get it I would try to repeat from memory what <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__2737" type="person">Dorothee</rs> wrote.</p>
                <closer><salute>Very sincerely yours</salute><signed><rs
                            ref="#tillich_person_id__3453" type="person">Toni Sawitz</rs></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
